      "body": "## Problem\n\nIn `megatron/core/tensor_parallel/layers.py`, `torch.amp.custom_fwd/custom_bwd` is created with a hardcoded `device_type=\"cuda\"`:\n\n```python\ncustom_fwd = partial(torch.amp.custom_fwd, device_type=\"cuda\")\ncustom_bwd = partial(torch.amp.custom_bwd, device_type=\"cuda\")\n```\n\nOn non-CUDA accelerators (e.g. Ascend NPU), autocast uses a different `device_type` (e.g. `\"npu\"`). The hardcoded `\"cuda\"` means the custom forward/backward decorators never match the autocast context, and the AMP cast guard is effectively disabled on those backends.\n\n## Fix\n\nDynamically resolve the device type from `torch.accelerator.current_accelerator()`:\n\n```python\n_CUSTOM_FWD_DEVICE_TYPE = getattr(torch.accelerator.current_accelerator(), \"type\", \"cuda\")\ncustom_fwd = partial(torch.amp.custom_fwd, device_type=_CUSTOM_FWD_DEVICE_TYPE)\ncustom_bwd = partial(torch.amp.custom_bwd, device_type=_CUSTOM_FWD_DEVICE_TYPE)\n```\n\nThis follows the same pattern already used elsewhere in the codebase: `get_compute_units()` in `batch_invariant_kernels.py` already resolves the accelerator type via `getattr(torch.accelerator.current_accelerator(), \"type\", \"cpu\")`.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Verified on Ascend NPU that `getattr(torch.accelerator.current_accelerator(), \"type\", \"cuda\")` correctly returns `\"npu\"`\n- The fix mirrors the approach used in the existing `batch_invariant_kernels.py`\n- Not tested: full end-to-end Megatron-LM training on NPU (this changes only the import-time definition of `custom_fwd`/`custom_bwd`; the fallback paths via `torch.cuda.amp.custom_fwd` for pre-2.4.0 are unchanged)\n\n## Related\n\n- The project already uses `torch.accelerator.current_accelerator()` in `batch_invariant_kernels.py:206` and `:1792`\n",
      "changedFiles": 1,
