            "body": "@balasaajay @jaredcasper — could one of you take a look at this when you have a moment?\n\nThe AMP decorators in `megatron/core/tensor_parallel/layers.py` are created with `device_type=\"cuda\"`, so on any non-CUDA accelerator the autocast guard never matches the active autocast context. The patch resolves the type from `torch.accelerator.current_accelerator()`, the same way `get_compute_units()` in `batch_invariant_kernels.py` already does.\n\nHappy to adjust anything you'd like before this can move forward.",
